  "releaseNotes": "🎉 v1.0.0 - First Stable Release with SOLID Architecture\n\n⚠️ BREAKING CHANGES from alpha versions:\n- StoreComponent now requires utility services via DI\n  Migration: Add services.AddStoreUtilities() in Program.cs\n- Direct Store<T> constructor changed\n  Migration: Use StoreBuilder<T>.Create(state).Build() pattern\n\n✨ New Features:\n- SOLID-based architecture (SRP, ISP, DIP compliance)\n- Interface segregation: IStateReader, IStateWriter, IStateObservable\n- Dependency injection throughout for better testability\n- Structured logging with ILogger<T> (no more Console.WriteLine)\n- Convenience methods: AddStoreWithUtilities<T>()\n- Comprehensive XML documentation (1,655+ lines)\n\n🔧 Improvements:\n- 30% reduction in StoreComponent code (530 → 370 lines)\n- 25% reduction in Store code (274 → 206 lines)\n- Better separation of concerns\n- Enhanced testability with DI\n\n📚 Documentation:\n- Complete migration guide (MIGRATION.md)\n- Architecture documentation (docs/ARCHITECTURE_V2.md)\n- Updated examples and troubleshooting\n\nSee CHANGELOG.md for full details.",
